;; repr/rust's round trip's negative controls (doc/GATE-SURVEY.md, GTS81 (a), "As built: GT9's controls"; bin/repr-rust roundtrip,
;; arbace.repr.rust's judge-controls): each is a crossed pair of two keys of a run, both passing the level (a file of the corpus, as the
;; reports and the known files name it; at the interface level a crate). The :subject's printed side is judged by the level's own
;; comparison (compare-file for the tree and lines, and the pretty layout's trees; compare-text-file for the text; compare-crate for
;; rustdoc's JSON) against the :reference's original side, and must differ: `control ID fails as it must`. A control the level judges
;; equal fails the run (`control passed`), as does one the level cannot compare (`control not judged`: a file of the pair missing); one
;; whose keys the run does not have (another corpus, --only) or that does not pass the level itself is left, so a control for each
;; corpus sits here and only that corpus's run reads it. :levels (optional) names the levels it applies to (:tree, :pretty, :text, :iface).
;; No control is a file of the corpus, the report, the known files or the counts. Read with the Clojure reader.
[{:id "_control/core-bool-vs-borrow" :subject "core/src/bool.rs" :reference "core/src/borrow.rs" :levels [:tree :pretty :text]
  :why "std's core: two small modules, other trees, other lines, other text; the corpus' known file is empty"}
